DESCRIPTION >
    Phase 4c (Pattern A row-pull). Per-conversion, picks the last touchpoint's
    attribution fields, replacing the HogQL correlated self-join in
    lastTouchAttribution (api/lib/attribution-engine.js:103-163).
    Built as 3 INDEPENDENT `ASOF LEFT JOIN`s (one per field: utm_source/medium,
    ai_source) rather than a single join picking one touchpoint row, because
    HogQL's actual query computes argMax(column, timestamp) SEPARATELY per
    column — and ClickHouse's argMax SKIPS rows where the column being
    aggregated is NULL when finding the max. That means the live HogQL model
    can synthesize credit from DIFFERENT touchpoints for different fields when
    the chronologically-last touch has a null in one field but an earlier touch
    doesn't (verified empirically on the 4c fixture's visitor Y, see
    tinybird/PHASE4_4C_PLAN.md and the 4c report — NOT a hypothesis, confirmed
    against real fired data both in PostHog and via two failed/passed Tinybird
    query shapes). A single ASOF JOIN picking one whole touchpoint row does NOT
    reproduce this and was empirically WRONG on that case. This is a faithful,
    validated parity port — not a "more correct" rewrite; replicating HogQL's
    actual behavior (including this null-skip quirk) is the explicit Phase 4
    goal per the reconciliation contract.
    A-2 (a single nested LEFT JOIN + argMax, structurally mirroring HogQL's
    literal SQL) was tried first and rejected outright by Tinybird:
    "Unsupported JOIN ON conditions" on the mixed equality+inequality ON clause
    — confirms classic ClickHouse JOIN doesn't accept this shape; ASOF JOIN is
    required either way.
    SCOPE LIMIT: validated only for distinct_id == visitor_id (every producer
    used in the 4c fixture sets only anonymous_id, no separate visitor_id/
    user_id). Server-events.js's user_id-merge path can in principle diverge
    visitor_id from distinct_id (normalize.js:251-253) — NOT covered by this
    pipe's validation; deferred to the $identify / identity-reconciliation
    backlog item.
    NOT YET PUSHED (no `tb push`/`tb deploy` run — validated via read-only
    `tb --cloud sql` against the live schema only, per standing no-push rule).

TOKEN "phase4_last_touch_read" READ

NODE last_touch_by_site_node
SQL >
    %
    SELECT
        conv.event_id AS conversion_event_id,
        conv.distinct_id,
        conv.timestamp AS conversion_timestamp,
        src.utm_source,
        med.utm_medium,
        camp.utm_campaign,
        ai.ai_source
    FROM
    (
        SELECT event_id, distinct_id, visitor_id, timestamp
        FROM events
        WHERE site_id = {{ String(site_id, required=True) }}
          AND event_type = '$conversion'
          AND timestamp >= {{ DateTime(date_from, required=True) }}
          AND timestamp < {{ DateTime(date_to, required=True) }}
    ) AS conv
    ASOF LEFT JOIN
    (
        SELECT visitor_id, timestamp, utm_source FROM events_by_visitor
        WHERE site_id = {{ String(site_id, required=True) }}
          AND event_type = '$pageview' AND utm_source IS NOT NULL
    ) AS src ON conv.visitor_id = src.visitor_id AND src.timestamp <= conv.timestamp
    ASOF LEFT JOIN
    (
        SELECT visitor_id, timestamp, utm_medium FROM events_by_visitor
        WHERE site_id = {{ String(site_id, required=True) }}
          AND event_type = '$pageview' AND utm_medium IS NOT NULL
    ) AS med ON conv.visitor_id = med.visitor_id AND med.timestamp <= conv.timestamp
    ASOF LEFT JOIN
    (
        SELECT visitor_id, timestamp, utm_campaign FROM events_by_visitor
        WHERE site_id = {{ String(site_id, required=True) }}
          AND event_type = '$pageview' AND utm_campaign IS NOT NULL
    ) AS camp ON conv.visitor_id = camp.visitor_id AND camp.timestamp <= conv.timestamp
    ASOF LEFT JOIN
    (
        SELECT visitor_id, timestamp, ai_source FROM events_by_visitor
        WHERE site_id = {{ String(site_id, required=True) }}
          AND event_type = '$pageview' AND ai_source IS NOT NULL
    ) AS ai ON conv.visitor_id = ai.visitor_id AND ai.timestamp <= conv.timestamp
    ORDER BY conv.timestamp DESC

TYPE endpoint
